Keep save states' file paths valid when the app's data container moves

A save state stores where each open 3DS archive lives on the host: the save
data, extra data, SD card, NAND and system save folders (their mount_point,
base_path, sdmc_directory and nand_directory), the LayeredFS patch folders, the
3GX plugin path and the amiibo file. They were written as absolute host paths.
Azahar already has a mechanism for this (FileUtil::Path::make, which writes the
user directory as %CITRA_USER_DIR% and puts the current one back on load), but
only open files used it.

On iOS the app's data container is "<...>/Data/Application/<UUID>/", and the
UUID changes when the app is reinstalled or its data restored. On an iPhone 14
Pro (2026-10-19) a state written under one container was resumed under
another: from then on every save write the game made failed, mkdir "Operation
not permitted" under the old container and "failed to get a handle for archive
archive_id=0x00000004" (SaveData), about three errors a frame, and the in-game
save never reached the phone.

This writes those fields through FileUtil::Path::make, so new states hold
placeholders. A state written before this patch still holds absolute paths:
on load, a path naming an older "<...>/Data/Application/<UUID>" is moved to the
current one, where the same files now are. The file format is unchanged (a
plain string either way), so old states load as before.

diff --git a/src/common/file_util.cpp b/src/common/file_util.cpp
index 8ad7ca1..bd185fd 100644
--- a/src/common/file_util.cpp
+++ b/src/common/file_util.cpp
@@ -1055,8 +1055,35 @@ bool StringReplace(std::string& haystack, const std::string& a, const std::strin
     return true;
 }
 
+// The app's data container in a path, "<...>/Data/Application/<UUID>", or an empty view.
+// iOS gives an app a new container UUID when it is reinstalled or restored, so a path
+// written into a save state before that points at a container that no longer exists.
+static std::string_view ContainerPrefix(std::string_view path) {
+    static constexpr std::string_view marker = "/Data/Application/";
+    static constexpr std::size_t uuid_length = 36;
+    const auto at = path.find(marker);
+    if (at == std::string_view::npos || path.size() < at + marker.size() + uuid_length) {
+        return {};
+    }
+    return path.substr(0, at + marker.size() + uuid_length);
+}
+
+// A loaded path that still names an older container is moved to the current one, where
+// the same files now live. Paths written by a newer core are placeholders and never match.
+static void RebaseContainer(std::string& path) {
+    const auto old_prefix = ContainerPrefix(path);
+    const auto new_prefix = ContainerPrefix(GetUserPath(UserPath::UserDir));
+    if (old_prefix.empty() || new_prefix.empty() || old_prefix == new_prefix) {
+        return;
+    }
+    path = std::string(new_prefix) + path.substr(old_prefix.size());
+}
+
 std::string SerializePath(const std::string& input, bool is_saving) {
     auto result = input;
+    if (!is_saving) {
+        RebaseContainer(result);
+    }
     StringReplace(result, "%CITRA_ROM_FILE%", g_currentRomPath, is_saving);
     StringReplace(result, "%CITRA_USER_DIR%", GetUserPath(UserPath::UserDir), is_saving);
     StringReplace(result, "%CITRA_USER_SDMC%", GetUserPath(UserPath::SDMCDir), is_saving);
